Z||000000||85ZainoGT||12-23-2001||01:09 AM||||ok, I think I have posted this b4, but I have a different question now... whenever I go over about 60mph my front end starts to float, not good because I dont really have much(enough) control of the car to feel safe...  not feeling safe @ 60+mph isnt good... but anyways, could it be my ball joints? or rack bushing deals? I dont know enough about cars to know, but I need to fix it, anyone know how/what/where/$$$ I can fix it? thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 GT all the options :)<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpicNEW3bsmall2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||12-23-2001||02:36 AM||||Do you have good shock on it?  Bounce the front end up and down putting your weight into it...and see if it keeps bouncing when you let go.<P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||California Kid||12-23-2001||09:38 AM||||Could be a number of things, if you have a reliable front end shop that you can trust, take it in for an inspection. Everything that moves in the front end from wheel bearings, suspension, to steering is suspect. Also, some brand tires are known to want to "track" on any road imperfections.<p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 12-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||lou_dias||12-23-2001||09:44 AM||||steering rack and may also require new suspension bushings<P>does your steering will have lots of play when the car is stopped?  that would mean the rack...||||reg||1
Z||000004||Smoooooth GT||12-23-2001||11:08 AM||||If you do a hood scoop like Orief's it will help also...  It let's air through instead of forcing it 'under' the car.. just a thought!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                       <BR>      <P><A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>   <BR>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<BR>"Smoooooth GT"<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||6
Z||000005||Mach10||12-23-2001||11:36 AM||||Yeah, but at only 60mph, it sounds like suspension. Either something's way outta whack (alignment, or something's loose (tie rods, BJs, bushings).<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000006||California Kid||12-23-2001||12:41 PM||||This probably isn't it (more likely things stated above), but check to see if you have the little lip spoiler on the underside rear of the facia. It's stands down about 2 inches runs across the rear of the facia.<P>I'm only adding this item as a couple of guy's have reported front end lift with this part removed, speeds 60mph+. See post by Kasdan "Weigh Reduction" in Technical.||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||12-23-2001||03:29 PM||||A mentioned above... some tires can do odd things. <P>small alignment problems can be a big pain in the neck.<P>check your air pressure all around. a couple PSI one way or the other can affect this.<P>Obviously, suspension problems can cause this, but don't assume it's in the front. rear problems can feel like front problems under certain conditions.<P>The bounce test for shocks/struts isn't all that meaningfull. In most cases it will only tell you if one is completely out. The shocks can be quite worn and still pass that. If they are more than a few years old you may want to replace them even if they seem ok. If you still have OE struts, get rid of them ASAP. Factory struts were junk to start with. Old ones are worse yet. If they show any signs of leaking, replace them, especially gas units. Gas units leaking oil have also usually lost all thier gas charge.||||reg||1
